{"author":{"id":"8d7a7fea5b07a0d5d081edd516d55afeb51ce9c18b2b2be6ceb30eb17cd9b547"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794344260,"nonce":"oRCG0ba+mY4p9lgtHBUHu2mEZY8=","title":"fix(text): a text_input caret in the middle of text ignores the kerning before the next glyph","message":"The caret stood at the measured width of the text before it. At the end of the text that is exactly where the next character goes: on a German-layout probe (DejaVu Sans, 28 px, \"HHHHHHHH\") the caret's left edge lies within 0.3 px of origin plus the sum of advances, which is how an editor places it. The 2 to 4 px between the last glyph's ink and the caret that the probe shows is that glyph's right-side bearing plus anti-aliasing, not an offset.\n\nIn the middle of the text the prefix is measured alone, so the kerning pair between the last prefix character and the next one is missing: \"AVATAR To Wa\" at 12 px puts the caret 2.0 px right of where the glyph after \"T\" is drawn. Umlauts and \"Müller Wilhelm lilli ÄÖÜ\", \"ößäü mmm iii\" are within 0.5 px at 12, 14 and 28 px.\n\nThe caret now stands where the next glyph is drawn: measure(prefix + next) minus measure(next), and the width at the end of the text. A test compares it with the glyph positions of the whole text's layout.","files":null}]}